-- title:
--   Isomorphism criterion for separated exceptional triples
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Write $S_+=\{a,a+d,a+d+h\}$, $S_-=\{a,a-d,a-d+h\}$ and $A_\pm(x,y)=1$ if $y-x\in S_\pm$, and zero otherwise. Assume $h\ne0$, $2h=0$, $3d\in\{0,h\}$, and $a,d,h$ generate $G$. Assume also $a\notin\{a+d,a+d+h,a-d,a-d+h\}$ and $a+d\notin\{a-d,a-d+h\}$. For the directed Cayley relation $x\to x+s$ with $s$ in the chosen support,
--
--   $$\operatorname{Cay}(G,S_+)\cong\operatorname{Cay}(G,S_-)\iff\langle a,h\rangle\ne G.$$
--
--   The isomorphism is an arbitrary vertex bijection; no finiteness is required.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L821-L861, lines 821–861; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeIso_iff_nongeneration_of_separated

